  "narration": {
    "title": "Yankees Stack the Best Rotation and Bullpen",
    "intro": "It's a pitching day, and one team shows up twice. The Yankees now own the best rotation by starter ERA and the second-best bullpen, a rare double. Up top the arms belong to Milwaukee's Jacob Misiorowski, still in a league of his own.",
    "staff_lead": "New York leads the rotation board at a 3.38 ERA, a nose ahead of Detroit at 3.43; the Brewers sit third at 3.44 with the best WHIP of the group at 1.09.",
    "bullpen_lead": "Boston still runs the sturdiest relief corps at a 2.95 ERA, with the Yankees right behind at 3.07 to lock down their second appearance among the leaders.",
    "arms_lead": "Misiorowski remains the standout at a 97 form score, a 1.75 ERA and a 0.75 WHIP that has held steady all week. Behind him, Cam Schlittler (86 form, 2.19 ERA) gives the Yankees a name to match their staff ranking, while Chris Sale keeps humming at a 2.16 ERA.",
    "risers_lead": "Cade Cavalli was the week's lone climber on the form board, up five points to 61 \u2014 modest, but the only arm trending up when everyone else held or slipped."
  }
}